{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Declutter: drop the "recommended purchase" rows from the cart drawer,
  and keep the real upsells.

  WHAT IS BEING REMOVED. nc-recs renders TWO blocks of optional add-to-cart
  products, both built client-side by assets/nc-recs.js:

    #cart .nc-recs        -- "You may also like", sitting under the item list
    #cart .nc-recs-panel  -- "Add & save more", inside the checkout panel under
                             the order total

  Each row is a product with a price and its own Add button. They are the last
  thing above checkout, so a cart with two items reads as a small catalogue and
  the actual total gets pushed down.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY KEPT. The pg-unlock offer rows (#pg-unlock-slot /
  .pg-unlock -- "Buy 1 more, get 1 FREE", "Add a 2nd PocketBoy R36") are the
  store's own upsells and are untouched. So is everything else nc-recs does,
  which is most of what that file actually is: the compact drawer top and logo,
  the 120px line-item thumbnails, the bundle-savings progress bar (.nc-tiers),
  the slim free-shipping bar, the duplicate-price fix and the quantity stepper.
  That is why this hides two blocks instead of removing the nc-recs section --
  dropping the section would take the whole cart's styling with it.

  WHY CSS RATHER THAN STOPPING THE SCRIPT. nc-recs.js fetches the related
  products and injects these blocks on its own schedule, re-running as the cart
  changes. Racing it from another file to delete nodes would mean re-deleting
  them on every cart mutation -- the same fight that made the upsell rows swap
  places earlier in this project. display:none settles it once: the blocks never
  take up space no matter how often the script rebuilds them.

  Registered after nc-recs in overlay-group.json so these rules are emitted
  last; !important is belt and braces, since nc-recs styles the same selectors.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  #cart .nc-recs,
  #cart .nc-recs-panel{display:none !important}
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Declutter", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Cart Declutter"}]}
{% endschema %}
